   "text": "I read the structure region by region and wrote it as a single SMILES. Stereochemistry is only partly encoded.\n\n**Reading of the drawing**\n- **Cyclohexane ring:** it carries a hydroxyl, a methoxy group, and the vinyl link to the macrocycle.\n- **Vinyl link:** the alkene is trisubstituted, with a methyl on one carbon. The ring and the ester-bearing CH are trans across it.\n- **Macrocycle:** it runs through the ester CH\u2013O\u2013C(=O) into the pipecolate ring (N-acylated). That leads into the \u03b1-keto amide and the hemiketal pyran (OH, methyl, methoxy, ring O).\n- **Chain after the pyran:** from the pyran CH the chain runs CH(OMe), CH2, CH(OMe), CH2, then C(CH3)=CH. Between the pyran CH and the methyl-bearing alkene the drawing shows two methoxy-bearing CH carbons separated by one CH2.\n- **Second alkene:** the CH2 and the chain-bearing CH are trans across it.\n- **Side chain:** the chain-bearing CH continues to a ketone and then CH2\u2013CH(OH)\u2013CH(CH3), which closes back to the ester CH. The side chain is CH2CH2CH2\u2013S\u2013CH2\u2013CH(NH2)\u2013CO2H, taken as L-cysteine.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\nI included only the two alkene geometries and the cysteine centre, taken as the R (L-cysteine) configuration. The wedges and hashes on the other stereocentres were not legible enough to assign, so those centres carry no stereo marks.\n\nSMILES: COC1CC(CCC1O)/C=C(C)/C2OC(=O)C3CCCCN3C(=O)C(=O)C4(O)C(C)CC(OC)C(O4)C(OC)CC(OC)C/C(C)=C/C(CCCSC[C@H](N)C(=O)O)C(=O)CC(O)C2C"
